{
  "title": "Recommended Acts (Aamal) in Madinah and Its Mosques",
  "data": "Madinah and the Prophet's Mosque\nWhile you are in Madinah, pray as much as you can in the Holy Prophet's Mosque.\nThe best place to pray in it is the Rawdah, between the Prophet's tomb and his minbar.\nVisit the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) and the Imams of al-Baqi (a.s.) as often as you can every day: [Ziyarat of the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.)](AP2), [Ziyarat of the Imams of al-Baqi (a.s.)](AP8).\nWhenever your eyes fall on the Prophet's chamber, invoke blessings upon him.\nAs long as you are in Madinah, guard yourself against every sin and act of disobedience to Allah, and reflect on the honour of the city and of the Prophet's Mosque.\nGive as much in alms as you can in Madinah, above all in the Prophet's Mosque and to the Sayyids, the Prophet's descendants.\nStay in Madinah as long as you can.",
  "tabs": [
    "Masjid Quba\nPray the two-unit prayer of greeting the mosque (tahiyyat al-masjid).\nThen recite the [Tasbih al-Zahra](I9).\nThen recite [Ziyarat Jamia Saghira](G12), the comprehensive ziyarat that opens \"Peace be upon the friends of Allah and His chosen ones\".\nThen supplicate Allah with the long dua that opens \"Ya ka'inan qabla kulli shay'\" (O He Who existed before all things).",
    "Masjid al-Fath\nMasjid al-Fath is also called Masjid al-Ahzab. Pray two units in it, and after the prayer recite:\nيَا صَرِيْخَ الْمَكْرُوْبِيْنَ\nYAA SAREEKHAL MAKROOBEEN\nO He Who aids the aggrieved!\nوَيَا مُجِيْبَ دَعْوَةِ الْمُضْطَرِّيْنَ\nWA YAA MUJEEBA DA'WATIL MUDTARREEN\nO He Who answers the call of the distressed!\nوَيَا مُغِيْثَ الْمَهْمُوْمِيْنَ\nWA YAA MUGHEETHAL MAHMOOMEEN\nO He Who comes to the help of the grief-stricken!\nاكْشِفْ عَنِّيْ ضُرِّيْ وَهَمِّيْ وَكَرْبِيْ وَغَمِّيْ\nIKSHIF A'NNEE DURREE WA HAMMEE WA KARBEE WA GHAMMEE\nRemove from me my distress, my grief, my anguish and my sorrow,\nكَمَا كَشَفْتَ عَنْ نَبِيِّكَ صَلَّى اللّٰهُ عَلَيْهِ وَاٰلِهٖ هَمَّهٗ\nKAMAA KASHAFTA A'N NABIYYIKA SALLALLAAHU A'LAYHI WA AALIHEE HAMMAH\njust as You removed the grief of Your Prophet, Allah bless him and his Household,\nوَكَفَيْتَهٗ هَوْلَ عَدُوِّهٖ\nWA KAFAYTAHOO HAWLA A'DUWWIH\nand spared him the terror of his enemy.\nوَاكْفِنِيْ مَاۤ اَهَمَّنِيْ مِنْ اَمْرِ الدُّنْيَا وَالْاٰخِرَةِ\nWAKFINEE MAA AHAMMANEE MIN AMRID DUNYAA WAL AAKHIRAH\nAnd suffice me in whatever concerns me of the affairs of this world and the Hereafter,\nيَاۤ اَرْحَمَ الرَّاحِمِيْنَ\nYAA ARHAMAR RAAHIMEEN\nO Most Merciful of the merciful!",
    "Other Mosques and Houses\nPray two units in the Mashrabat Umm Ibrahim, the house of the mother of Ibrahim, the Holy Prophet's son.\nPray two units in Masjid al-Fadikh, also called Masjid Radd al-Shams, near Masjid Quba.\nIn the houses of Imam Zayn al-Abidin (a.s.) and Imam Ja'far al-Sadiq (a.s.), pray as much as you can and ask Allah for your needs.\nDo the same in Masjid Salman, in the mosque of Amir al-Mu'minin (a.s.) facing [the tomb of Hamzah (a.s.)](AQ2), and in Masjid al-Mubahalah."
  ],
  "merits": "Madinah and the Prophet's Mosque: Shaykh Abbas al-Qummi writes, as he had in his Hadiyyat al-Za'irin, that visitors to Madinah should seize the chance of their stay to pray as much as they can in the Holy Prophet's Mosque, for one prayer there equals ten thousand prayers elsewhere, and that the best place in it is the Rawdah, between the Prophet's tomb and his minbar.\n\nHis teacher writes in Tahiyyat al-Za'ir that the places where the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) and the Imams (a.s.) are buried are more honourable even than Makkah; the scholars agree on this, as al-Shahid al-Awwal states in al-Qawa'id wa al-Fawa'id.\n\nIn a sound (hasan) narration, al-Hadrami reports that Imam al-Sadiq (a.s.) told him to pray as much as he could in the Prophet's Mosque, for he would not always have the chance to be in that holy place.\n\nIn Tahdhib al-Ahkam, Shaykh al-Tusi reports with a reliable chain from Murazim that Imam al-Sadiq (a.s.) said: \"Fasting in Madinah and praying at the pillars of the Prophet's Mosque are not obligatory; what is obligatory is only the five daily prayers and the fast of the month of Ramazan. Yet whoever wishes may fast there, for it is good for him. Pray as much as you can in this mosque, for that is good for you. Know that a man who is skilful in the affairs of this world is praised for it; how then of one who is skilful in the affairs of his Hereafter?\"\n\nMadinah and its mosque are the footsteps of the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.): he walked its streets and markets and prayed in its mosques. It is the place where the revelation came down, and where Gabriel and the angels nearest to Allah descended. A poet says of it: \"A land in whose courtyards Gabriel walked; Allah has honoured its earth and its sky.\"\n\nAlms given in Madinah, and in the Prophet's Mosque above all, bring an immense reward, especially when given to the Sayyids. Allamah al-Majlisi says that a reliable narration reports that one dirham given in alms in Madinah equals ten thousand dirhams given elsewhere.\n\nStaying in Madinah is recommended, and many narrations speak of its merit.\n\nMasjid Quba: it is the mosque \"founded on piety from the very first day\" ([Surah At-Tawbah](A13), 9:108). It is narrated that two units of prayer in it bring the reward of an umrah. The dua \"Ya ka'inan qabla kulli shay'\" is long, and Shaykh Abbas al-Qummi leaves it out of Mafatih al-Jinan for brevity; Allamah al-Majlisi records it in Bihar al-Anwar.\n\nMashrabat Umm Ibrahim: the house of the mother of Ibrahim, the Holy Prophet's son, was the Prophet's own home and place of prayer."
